`ρ_k = β_k + i γ_k` of `ζ` with `5000 < γ_k ≤ 6000` (zeros number 4521 to 5598), as computed by
Arb (`acb_dirichlet_zeta_zeros`, 160-bit ball arithmetic). Copied from the lists `ord0`, `ord1`, …
of `challenge/Zeros5000to6000.lean` in `Garald1/zeta-zero-locations`; only the names and the line
breaks differ. The list is data: the conclusions of `ZetaZeroLocations.v6` say what is true of
it, and nothing may assume it is correct. Chunks of at most 300 entries, as in the source.
